    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0497" n="1331" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 659.119/354</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grant-Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-06T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>958. Your 2452, June 29, noon. Whenever in your sound discretion it appears
                    advisable, War Trade Board will license for prompt shipment 2,000 tons wrought
                    iron tubing, and if you find it will be of service in the situation described in
                    your wire you may intimate that at your request we would be willing to go
                    further in iron and steel materials.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
